# Make the llm-emu plugin run against vLLM v0.34.0.
#
# The plugin targets vLLM 0.18.1 upstream and patches 01-04 carried it to
# v0.29.0.  Its patches still applied and its modules still imported at
# v0.34.0, so the build was green, but an emulated serve died on the first
# request and had lost its model-runner stubs before that.  Each item below is
# a vLLM internal that moved, with what it broke.  Every change keeps the older
# code path beside the new one; that older path was not re-run on v0.29.0.
#
# 1. ModelRunnerOutput.req_id_to_index  (hooks/executor_hook.py)
#    v0.34.0 removed the field; the scheduler derives the index from req_ids.
#    The hook still passed it, so the first scheduled step raised
#      TypeError: ModelRunnerOutput.__init__() got an unexpected keyword
#      argument 'req_id_to_index'
#    inside execute_model(), which kills the engine core (EngineDeadError, HTTP
#    500 on every request).  Pass it only when the dataclass has it.
#
# 2. vllm.v1.worker.gpu_model_runner is gone  (cuda_mock.py)
#    v0.34.0 has one model runner, vllm.v1.worker.gpu.model_runner, built by
#    Worker._make_model_runner().  The import hook that stubs
#    GPUModelRunner.load_model/profile_run/_dummy_run/get_model was armed for
#    the old module name and never fired, and the init_device fallback imported
#    the old module too, so it fell through to the do-nothing _StubRunner.  Arm
#    the hook for both module names and build the fallback runner through the
#    worker's factory when it has one.
#
# 3. Worker.init_device never completed  (platform.py, cuda_mock.py)
#    By the v0.29.0 source it did not complete there either -- set_random_seed()
#    calls current_platform.manual_seed_all(), which EmulatorPlatform did not
#    implement -- and emulation worked because the fallback in (2) rebuilt the
#    runner after the distributed groups were already up.  At v0.34.0 three
#    things stand between it and a real, fully initialised worker:
#      - Platform.manual_seed_all() raises NotImplementedError: implement it.
#      - MemorySnapshot unpacks torch.accelerator.get_memory_info(), which the
#        catch-all accelerator shim answered with None: return (free, total).
#      - Worker._maybe_get_memory_pool_context() resolves a sleep-mode
#        allocator by platform and raises for anything that is not CUDA-alike,
#        XPU or CPU: the emulator allocates nothing, so use no pool.
#    With these init_device runs to the end and the fallback is not taken.  The
#    fallback message now names the exception type, since the ones that reach
#    it (NotImplementedError, AssertionError) usually carry no text.
#
# 4. KV connector cycle  (hooks/executor_hook.py)
#    The worker-side connector lifecycle the hook reproduces moved from
#    KVConnectorModelRunnerMixin to ActiveKVConnector
#    (vllm/v1/worker/gpu/kv_connector.py) and grew: handle_preemptions() before
#    bind, finish_forward() after the forward, and get_transfer_results() in
#    place of get_finished(), which also reports failed receives
#    (KVConnectorOutput.failed_recving, read by the scheduler).  Follow that
#    order, falling back to get_finished() where the newer call is absent.
#
# 5. CacheConfig.gpu_memory_utilization may be None  (cuda_mock.py,
#    profiler/trace_profiler.py)
#    v0.34.0 leaves it unset unless the flag is given and exposes the effective
#    value as resolved_gpu_memory_utilization.  The heuristic KV-pool estimate
#    (packs without available_kv_cache_bytes) did float(None), and a captured
#    trace header recorded null.  Read the resolved value.
#
# 6. Worker.initialize_from_config  (cuda_mock.py)
#    The real method now also copies hash_block_size and
#    cache_hit_alignment_tokens from the KVCacheConfig onto the worker's cache
#    config; the stub that replaces it does the same.
#
diff --git a/vllm_emulator/cuda_mock.py b/vllm_emulator/cuda_mock.py
index 49ee38c..8522999 100644
--- a/vllm_emulator/cuda_mock.py
+++ b/vllm_emulator/cuda_mock.py
